    topicCode: 'SS2-VA-05',
    module: 'Design and Applied Arts',
    term: 'First Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Graphic design</span> combines art and communication, using visual elements to convey messages effectively. This lesson introduces the meaning, types, tools, and practical applications of graphic design.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning and Types of Graphic Design</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Graphic design</span> is the art of visually communicating ideas or messages using a combination of images, typography, colour, and layout. It is applied across a range of practical products.</p>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type/Application</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Book cover design</td><td>Visual design for the front cover of a book, meant to attract readers and convey the book\'s content</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Book jacket design</td><td>The removable, printed paper cover that wraps around a hardcover book, similar in function to a book cover</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Logo design</td><td>A simple, memorable graphic symbol representing a company, brand, or organization</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Calendar design</td><td>Layout combining dates with visual imagery, often for promotional or decorative purposes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Poster design</td><td>A large-format visual designed to advertise an event, product, or message</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Packaging design</td><td>The visual and structural design of a product\'s container/wrapping</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Tools and Materials for Graphic Design</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Traditional graphic design tools include pencils, rulers, set squares, drawing pens, markers, and paper/board. Modern graphic design also relies heavily on computer software and digital tools for creating and refining designs.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Calligraphy in Graphic Design</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Calligraphy</span> is the art of beautiful, decorative handwriting or lettering. It is often used in graphic design for logos, invitations, book covers, and other designs where elegant, stylized text adds visual appeal and character.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Practical Application of Graphic Design</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Graphic designers apply principles of layout, balance, contrast, and typography to create effective book covers, logos, calendars, posters, and packaging that communicate a clear message while remaining visually appealing to the target audience.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember: a book cover is the printed cover itself, while a book jacket is a separate, removable paper wrap placed OVER a hardcover book — they are related but distinct.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Graphic design uses images, typography, colour, and layout to communicate visually, applied in book covers, jackets, logos, calendars, posters, and packaging. Calligraphy — decorative lettering — is an important skill within graphic design practice.\n</div>\n  ',
