    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  <span class="learn-keyword">Construction</span>, as an art form, involves building three-dimensional objects by joining together various materials. This lesson introduces the meaning, types, processes, and materials involved in artistic construction.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Construction (as an Art Form)</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">In visual arts, <span class="learn-keyword">construction</span> refers to the process of creating three-dimensional art objects by assembling, joining, or combining different materials together, rather than carving away material (as in sculpture) or shaping a single moldable substance (as in pottery).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Types of Construction</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Additive construction</td><td>Building up a form by adding and joining pieces together</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Assemblage</td><td>Combining found objects or materials into a unified artwork</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Mixed-media construction</td><td>Combining multiple different types of materials (e.g., wood, metal, fabric) in a single piece</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Objects and Materials Used in Construction</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A wide variety of materials can be used in artistic construction, including <strong>hard board</strong>, <strong>beads</strong>, <strong>metal</strong>, and <strong>rope</strong>, among others. The choice of material affects the texture, weight, durability, and overall visual character of the finished construction.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Processes Involved in Construction</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The construction process typically involves planning the design, selecting and preparing appropriate materials, cutting or shaping pieces as needed, and joining the pieces together using appropriate methods (such as gluing, tying, welding, or fastening) to build the final three-dimensional artwork.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember: construction is about JOINING/ASSEMBLING separate materials together, unlike carving (removing material) or modelling/pottery (shaping one moldable substance).\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Construction, as an art form, involves creating three-dimensional works by assembling and joining various materials such as hard board, beads, metal, and rope, following a process of planning, material preparation, cutting, and joining to produce a finished piece.\n</div>\n  ',
