    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Computers have become an essential tool in modern visual arts practice, from graphic design to digital illustration. This lesson introduces computer basics, key hardware, and the use of design software like CorelDraw in visual arts.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning and Types of Computers</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A <span class="learn-keyword">computer</span> is an electronic device that processes data according to a set of instructions (software) to perform tasks, including tasks relevant to visual arts such as digital drawing, image editing, and design layout. Types of computers include desktops, laptops, and tablets, each offering different levels of portability and processing power for art-related tasks.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Parts and Functions of a Computer</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Function</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Monitor</td><td>Displays visual output, essential for viewing and editing artwork</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Keyboard</td><td>Allows text input and command shortcuts</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Mouse/graphics tablet</td><td>Allows precise cursor control, essential for digital drawing and design</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CPU (Central Processing Unit)</td><td>The "brain" of the computer, processing instructions and running software</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Storage drive</td><td>Stores files, including artwork and design projects, for later access</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Drives and Printers</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Drives</strong> (such as hard drives, external drives, and flash drives) store digital files, including artwork. A <strong>printer</strong> converts a digital design into a physical, printed output — essential for producing tangible copies of digital designs such as posters, book covers, or packaging mockups.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. CorelDraw Window and Tools</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">CorelDraw</span> is a popular vector graphic design software used widely in graphic design and visual arts. Its interface (window) includes a toolbox (with tools for drawing shapes, selecting objects, and applying colour), a canvas/workspace (where the design is created), and menus for file management and editing options.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">5. Advantages and Disadvantages of Computer Use in Art</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Advantages</th><th>Disadvantages</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Allows easy editing, undoing, and experimentation without wasting materials</td><td>Requires access to expensive equipment and software</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Enables precise, scalable, and reproducible designs</td><td>Can reduce reliance on traditional hand skills if overused</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Speeds up repetitive design tasks</td><td>Technical issues (power outages, software crashes) can disrupt work</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember that CorelDraw is a vector-based design software commonly used for graphic design tasks like logos and posters — a frequently tested software name in visual arts exams.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Computers are important tools in modern visual arts, with parts like the monitor, keyboard, and CPU supporting digital design work. Software like CorelDraw provides tools for graphic design, while drives store files and printers produce physical output — offering both advantages (precision, easy editing) and disadvantages (cost, technical disruptions).\n</div>\n  ',
