    term: 'Third Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  The <span class="learn-keyword">calabash</span> — a dried, hollowed gourd — has been used across Nigeria for centuries, both as a practical vessel and as a canvas for decorative art. This lesson introduces the calabash, its types, decoration methods, and functions.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning and Types of Calabash</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A <span class="learn-keyword">calabash</span> is the dried, hollowed-out shell of a gourd (usually from the bottle gourd plant), used traditionally as a container or vessel. Calabashes vary in shape and size — some are round and bowl-like, while others are elongated with a narrow neck, suited to different practical or decorative uses.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Types of Calabash Decoration</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Painted decoration</td><td>Applying colour and designs directly onto the calabash surface</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Engraved/carved decoration</td><td>Cutting or scratching designs into the surface of the calabash</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Beaded decoration</td><td>Attaching beads to the calabash surface in decorative patterns</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Burnt/pyro-engraved decoration</td><td>Using heat to burn decorative patterns into the calabash surface</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Uses and Functions of Decorated Calabash</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Decorated calabashes serve functions including storage (of grain, water, or other items), serving food or drink during ceremonies, use as musical instruments (e.g., percussion), display as decorative art objects, and as symbols of status or ceremonial importance in various Nigerian cultures.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Marketing and Outlets for Calabash Products</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Decorated calabash products are marketed and sold through local markets, craft fairs, souvenir shops, and increasingly through online platforms, targeting both local buyers seeking traditional and ceremonial items, and tourists interested in authentic Nigerian craft art.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Learn the distinct decoration methods — painted, engraved/carved, beaded, and burnt/pyro-engraved — as these are often tested individually with descriptive scenarios.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> A calabash is a dried, hollowed gourd used traditionally as a vessel, decorated through methods such as painting, engraving, beading, or burning. Decorated calabashes serve functions from storage to ceremonial use, and are marketed through markets, craft fairs, and other outlets.\n</div>\n  ',
