    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Basket and mat weaving is one of Nigeria\'s most widespread indigenous crafts, combining practicality with artistic skill. This lesson examines the materials, techniques, and uses of traditional basket and mat making.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of Basket and Mat Making</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><span class="learn-keyword">Basket and mat making</span> is the craft of weaving natural plant fibres into functional and decorative objects — baskets for carrying or storage, and mats for sitting, sleeping, or covering surfaces.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Materials Used</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Common materials include <strong>raffia</strong> (fibre from the raffia palm), <strong>cane/rattan</strong>, <strong>palm fronds</strong>, and various grasses and reeds — all locally sourced, flexible plant materials suited to weaving.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Weaving Techniques</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Plaiting</td><td>Interlacing three or more strands of fibre in a criss-cross pattern</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coiling</td><td>Wrapping and stitching a coiled fibre bundle into a spiral shape to build up a form</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Twining</td><td>Twisting pairs of weft fibres around rigid warp fibres to bind them together</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Wicker/basket weaving</td><td>Weaving rigid materials over and under a rigid frame to create a sturdy structure</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Functions and Uses of Baskets and Mats</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Baskets serve functions such as carrying farm produce, storing grain, and general household storage, while mats are used for sitting, sleeping, drying agricultural produce in the sun, and as decorative floor or wall coverings. Both items may also be dyed or patterned for additional decorative and cultural significance.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know your weaving techniques: plaiting (criss-cross interlacing), coiling (spiral wrapping), twining (twisting weft around warp), and wicker weaving (over-and-under on a frame).\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Basket and mat making weaves natural fibres like raffia, cane, and palm fronds using techniques such as plaiting, coiling, twining, and wicker weaving, producing functional items used for carrying, storage, sitting, sleeping, and decoration.\n</div>\n  ',
